claw2 — a personal AI agent you host yourself

It works with the language-model provider of your choice and keeps
conversations, files and long-term memory on your own machine. Beyond its
built-in tools it delegates to skills: small Node.js scripts the agent can
write itself and run after your confirmation.

On FreeBSD this port runs the gateway natively (no Docker): the gateway,
the web interface and the mobile web client, with the skills in the soft
sandbox — the Node.js permission model plus the egress guard. Local ONNX
embeddings and the privacy-OCR and SIP sidecars are not available here.

This port lives outside the official ports tree on purpose: its build
fetches the application's npm dependencies from the registry instead of
listing them as distfiles. Source of the application and of this packaging:
